@baseUrl = http://localhost:5032
@medxToken = REPLACE_WITH_MEDX_JWT

### Get an order directly from LIS; no local database changes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/order/MR2610-00001
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}

### Nonexistent order: LIS normally returns HTTP 200 with result: null
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/order/NONEXISTENT_TEST_CENTREID
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}

### Update LIS order fields from latest local data (external PATCH /api/UpdateOrder/)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/updateorder
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "centreId": "MR2610-00001"
}

### Update LIS patient fields from latest local data (external PATCH /api/UpdateOrderPatient/)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/updateorderpatient
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "centreId": "MR2610-00001"
}

### Blank centreid: 400, no LIS update
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/updateorderpatient
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "centreId": " "
}

### Prepare and preview orders without calling LIS (writes centreid and pending queue rows)
# Uses the system JWT; LIS authentication uses server-configured credentials.
# Accepts only SequenceDate, FormTypes and Status; no shared order parameters required.
# The three parameters control centreid generation and queue preparation.
# SequenceDate and FormTypes also filter returned records by sequence_date and formtype.
# FormTypes is a non-empty array passed to p_formtypes text[]; defaults to ["DR"].
# Each entry must be non-blank and at most 2 characters; null/empty arrays are rejected.
# Then returns ALL columns of patientdetails_sync for that date and those form types, ordered by id.
# No target-system or synchronization-state filter is applied to the response.
# Matching already synchronized rows are included; null sequence_date rows are excluded.
# Response contains totalCount and results; no patient payload or validation counts.
# Actual createorders still sends only pending records.
# Does not claim queue rows, increment attempt_count or change synchronization status.
# This is a snapshot, not a reservation or guarantee of remote LIS validation.
# SequenceDate is optional and defaults to database CURRENT_DATE.
# Gaps or duplicates blocking centreid generation return HTTP 409 ProblemDetails.
# detail contains the business error only, without PostgreSQL CONTEXT or stack traces.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/createorders/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "SequenceDate": "2026-10-28",
  "FormTypes": ["DR", "DC"],
  "Status": "Matched"
}

### Synchronize DR and DC / Matched patients: submit create directly
# Does not query existing orders; an exact same-LabId duplicate counts as succeeded.
# Duplicate confirms the order exists, but does not update order or patient data.
# Request exposes only SequenceDate, FormTypes and Status.
# referringDoctorCode uses refcustordr; BillingDoctorCode uses billtocustordr.
# Missing database doctor codes fail validation before submission.
# SiteCode uses Lis:SiteCode; Priority=R and PaymentOption=A.
# createdBy uses users.username; TestProfiles maps patientdetails_final.productcode,
# with IsBillable=true. DOB is sent with AgeType=AGE when present.
# Generates centreid using update_patientdetails_final_centreid, then reads
# get_patientdetails_final_pending_sync. CreatedBy comes from users.username.
# centreid is sent as LabId; the returned result.LabId is saved as remote_record_id.
# Only pending LIS synchronization records are submitted. Stops on the first failure.
# HTTP 207 means a failure occurred; inspect Results and UnprocessedCount.
# Patients are sent with AgeType=AGE and AgeUnit=Y.
# Batch synchronization currently omits Patient.HKID.
# SequenceDate is optional; when omitted, the database CURRENT_DATE is used.
# Results include SyncId and CentreId. TotalCount includes only selected pending rows.
# SkippedCount is zero because non-pending records are excluded by the function.
# Sending claims each pending row as in_progress and increments attempt_count.
# Success sets succeeded, synced_at and remote_record_id; rejection sets failed.
# Uncertain outcomes set unknown; stale in_progress also requires reconciliation.
# Failed/unknown records are not automatically retried; review before resetting to pending.
# Do not retry an uncertain LIS submission without checking LIS first.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/createorders
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "SequenceDate": "2026-10-28",
  "FormTypes": ["DR", "DC"],
  "Status": "Matched"
}

### Request an LIS token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/token
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=REPLACE_WITH_LIS_USERNAME&password=REPLACE_WITH_URL_ENCODED_PASSWORD&grant_type=password

### Request an LIS token using configured defaults
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/token
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

### Request an LIS token using configured defaults (GET, no parameters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/token
Authorization: ******

### Synchronize one LIS order by submitting a create request directly
# Does not query the remote order or update existing order/patient data.
# Selects a unique patient by CentreId + TargetSystem through patientdetails_sync.
# Only LIS is supported; other target systems return 400 before any submission.
# Patient, DailyNo and CreatedBy come from patientdetails_final and users.
# ReferringDoctorCode uses refcustordr; BillingDoctorCode uses billtocustordr.
# Missing database doctor codes fail validation before submission.
# Request exposes only CentreId and TargetSystem, with no shared order parameters.
# Uses server defaults: SiteCode=LAB, Priority=R, PaymentOption=A.
# TestProfiles and Samples are omitted.
# HKID is omitted, consistently with batch synchronization.
# No match returns 404; ambiguous matches or non-pending state return 409.
# Only pending records may be sent; LabId is populated from the queued centreid.
# A LIS error "Duplicate Data: <same centreid>" counts as already synchronized.
# Supports plain text, a JSON string or a JSON error object, including HTTP 200 responses.
# Returns 200 with alreadySynced=true; saves succeeded, synced_at and remote_record_id.
# The original LIS HTTP status is retained in last_http_status; batches continue.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/createorder
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "CentreId": "MR2610-00001",
  "TargetSystem": "LIS"
}

### Retry one failed or unknown LIS order using current patientdetails_final data
# The synchronization status belongs to patientdetails_sync, not patientdetails_final.
# Request exposes only CentreId and TargetSystem, with no shared order parameters.
# Uses the same patient selection, database mapping and order validation as createorder.
# Other order parameters use server defaults (SiteCode=LAB, Priority=R, PaymentOption=A).
# Does not regenerate centreid; sends the original centreid as LabId.
# Directly submits CreateOrder without checking the remote order first.
# A duplicate confirms order existence only, not that patient data was updated.
# Atomically claims failed/unknown -> in_progress and increments attempt_count.
# Other states (pending/succeeded/in_progress) return 409 without submitting.
# Unknown retries reuse the original LabId so LIS uniqueness prevents duplicate orders.
# Success or an exact same-LabId duplicate saves succeeded and remote_record_id.
# Rejection saves failed; uncertain outcomes save unknown and require reconciliation.
# Does not reset the row to pending or automatically retry other records.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Lis/createorder/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{medxToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "CentreId": "MR2610-00002",
  "TargetSystem": "LIS"
}